I ordered half a pork banh mi with everything on it and it was reminiscent of the Vietnamese spots in the east bay suburbs. My only complaint is their bread isn't as flaky and it's more soft and dense, but it does the job for a craving. They didn't skimp out on the pork which is good. 

The lady running the counter was really nice and I got my sandwich way faster than I'd expect anywhere else in this area. Worth it!"},{"review_date":"2017-03-15 18:18:55","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Freshest sandwich in town. The bread is so soft and the ingredients are so fresh. Never greasy, light yet filling. So delicious! My favorite is the pastrami, it's the Wednesday special. If you like your sandwich with everything make sure you let them know or they won't put condiments on it. Must try!"}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"888 Embarcadero Del N","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":true,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":false,"street":true,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":false,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":null},"business_stars":4.0,"categories":"Hot Dogs, Restaurants","city":"Isla Vista","hours":{"Friday":"11:0-3:0","Monday":"11:0-22:0","Saturday":"11:0-3:0","Sunday":"11:0-22:0","Thursday":"11:0-3:0","Tuesday":"11:0-22:0","Wednesday":"11:0-22:0"},"name":"Dogtown","review_info":[{"review_date":"2012-06-28 16:27:59","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"Had a BBQ Burger and Crisscut fries from this location which was very delicious. However, this restaurant is no longer here and is being replaced with The Habit Burger [!!!!]."},{"review_date":"2012-06-14 00:40:03","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"This is my favorite place in Isla Vista hands down.  Not only are the hotdogs/sausages great but their burgers are surprisingly the cheapest and most delicious in town!  It does not end there, the sweet potatoe fries are AMAZINGLY delicious, affordable and plentiful!"},{"review_date":"2012-04-11 03:18:49","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"This place was a go-to when I lived in Isla Vista.  I'd always go for hotdog, sourkraut and mustard, simple and delicious. 

What really sets this place a part from your average hot-dog joint are the dogtown fries.  Think of them as Nacho fries.  They are so amazing.  The fries are loaded with beans, guacamole, onions, jalapenos, grated cheese, & bacon bits.  

These alone give them 4/5 stars. The missing star is the price (but really, what isn't over priced in Isla Vista) and for being a hot dog place, I really wish the hot dogs were amazing instead of okay."}],"state":"CA"}

